xnu 0100: flush the console ring and the sampler from the UFS write path

tsleep() timeouts stop waking kernel threads once userland starts on this
board: the sampler prints its first line and the log writer flushes the first
137 lines, then neither ever runs again (measured with the corrected dump).
Neither can be paced by a timer. Flush the ring from
mondrian_ufs_strategy() whenever 32 KiB are pending (try_lock, so an I/O in
progress only defers it) and take one sampler line every 256 calls of the same
hook. The writer thread stays as the first-flush/fallback path.

